#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:20
msgid ""
"Client libraries in ROS provide the APIs that developers use to create "
"nodes, communicate between processes, and access core system functionality. "
"This article explains the supported client libraries, how they relate to "
"lower-level ROS interfaces, and how they enable development in different "
"programming languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:37
msgid ""
"Client libraries are the APIs that allow you to implement your ROS code. "
"This article explains ``rcl``, the shared core library, and the main C++ and "
"Python client libraries. With this information, you can choose the right "
"library for your language and understand how nodes written in different "
"languages work together."
msgstr ""

