#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:151
msgid "FAQs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:153
msgid "What is a client library?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:154
msgid ""
"A client library is the API you use to write ROS code in a given programming "
"language. It gives you access to core ROS concepts such as nodes, topics, "
"services, parameters, and logging."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:157
msgid "Can nodes written with different client libraries communicate?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:158
msgid ""
"Yes. Client libraries generate language bindings for ROS interface files, so "
"nodes can share messages even when they use different languages, for example "
"``rclcpp`` and ``rclpy``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:161
msgid "What is the ROS Client Library (``rcl``)?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:162
msgid ""
"``rcl`` is the common C core that implements language-independent ROS "
"behaviour, such as parameters and namespaces. Language-specific client "
"libraries wrap ``rcl`` instead of reimplementing that shared logic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:165
msgid "Why does ROS use a common ``rcl`` core?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:166
msgid ""
"Shared behaviour stays consistent across languages, and bug fixes or "
"behaviour changes in ``rcl`` apply to every client library that uses it. "
"That also keeps the language-specific libraries thinner and easier to "
"maintain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:169
msgid "Is all client library behaviour implemented in ``rcl``?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/About-Client-Libraries.rst:170
msgid ""
"No. Features that depend on the programming language, such as the threading "
"model used by spin functions, are implemented in each client library rather "
"than in ``rcl``."
msgstr ""
